The raw readback preserves the policy byte, but the expected output is wrong: the inspected GnuPG 2.4 sources encode the second byte as `+`, so expect `S UIF-1 %02+`. The card-only boot now sets both variables. I’m checking the rehearsal’s media reuse and acceptance steps next.
